id: pm-context-qu0a
title: Alert on daily release failure and require merge drivers in CI
description: "Two CI fixes: release.yml gains an if:failure() job that opens or updates one deduplicated tracking issue (label release-failure, stable title) with job name, run URL, commit SHA and date, issues:write only; ci.yml installs pm merge drivers before the health gate and passes --require-merge-drivers so a fresh clone fails the gate instead of silently passing. Motivated by five unnoticed failed daily releases since 2026-08-17."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-22T19:02:21.960Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-22T19:02:36.190Z"
assignee: ox-alpha
claim_principal: ox-alpha
author: ox-alpha
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T19:02:33.172Z",ox-alpha,"Gate proof: removed all five merge.pm-* config sections, ./node_modules/.bin/pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers exited 1; after ./node_modules/.bin/pm merge install it exited 0. Plain --strict-exit stays 0 both ways."
files[2]{path,scope}:
  .github/workflows/ci.yml,project
  .github/workflows/release.yml,project
tests[2]{command,path,scope,note}:
  python3 .agents/pm/verify-release-yaml.py,.github/workflows/release.yml,project,"release.yml parses; alert-on-release-failure job has if: failure(), needs release, permissions issues:write"
  git config --local --remove-section merge.pm-item-toon && ./node_modules/.bin/pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers,.,project,health gate exits non-zero when clone-local merge drivers are absent
body: ""
